{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec66e52411ba563376289d729c0707d222b165e9b0fbaeb722b12c8be5b6acd1","digest":{"component_or_area":"metrics snapshot writer/reader","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/snapshot.py","write_snapshot()","read_snapshots()",".rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson",".gitignore","tests/unit/metrics/test_snapshot.py",".rebar/"],"problem_keywords":["metrics snapshot","NDJSON","persistence","trend tracking","git tracking","gitignore"],"propositions":["Metrics snapshot records (coverage, complexity, clone count) computed at CI runtime are not persisted; a durable append-only NDJSON store is needed to accumulate trend history.","The snapshot file must live under .rebar/ (a tracked directory) and not under reports/ (which is gitignored), so trend snapshots are committed and synced across runs.","A gitignore negation rule (!.rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson) must be added to surgically un-ignore the snapshot file despite the blanket .rebar/* rule.","write_snapshot(dict) appends timestamped records to the NDJSON file; read_snapshots(since, until) yields in-range records; malformed lines are skipped without error."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787773136233326001,"uuid":"a5bcfad5-879f-43b9-ba4e-94932109c3b8"}